    {
      "extracted_at": "2026-09-01T01:46:57Z",
      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2",
              "years": "2025, 2024, 2023"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "(thousands of oil-equivalent barrels daily)\nOil-equivalent production\t4,736\t4,333\t3,738",
            "entity_name": "XOM Total Upstream E&P",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "At year-end 2025, approximately 7.0 billion oil-equivalent barrels (GOEB) of ExxonMobil's proved reserves were classified as proved undeveloped. This represents 36 percent of the 19.3 GOEB reported in proved reserves. This compares to 7.4 GOEB of proved undeveloped reserves reported at the end of 2024.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Total Upstream E&P",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Overall, investments of $19.0 billion were made by the Corporation during 2025 to progress the development of reported proved undeveloped reserves, including $18.8 billion for oil and gas producing activities, along with additional investments for other non-oil and gas producing activities such as the construction of support infrastructure and other related facilities.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Total Upstream E&P",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "During the year, development activities focused on liquids-rich opportunities in the onshore U.S., primarily in the Permian Basin of West Texas and New Mexico, bringing total U.S. net production to 2.1 million oil-equivalent barrels per day. Development activities also continued on the Golden Pass LNG export project, including mechanical completion of Train 1 in late 2025.",
            "entity_name": "XOM United States Upstream",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Total operations in Canada provided 519 thousand oil-equivalent barrels per day in net production, where oil and gas operations are active onshore in Alberta and offshore in Newfoundland and Labrador.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Canada Upstream",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "During 2025, average net production at Kearl was about 264 thousand barrels per day.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Kearl Oil Sands Operations",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "In 2025, the Company's share of net production of synthetic crude oil was about 68 thousand barrels per day and share of net acreage was about 55 thousand acres in the Athabasca oil sands deposit.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Syncrude Operations",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In 2025, ExxonMobil exited Thailand operations, while production activities continued throughout the region.",
            "entity_name": "XOM 2025 Thailand Upstream Exit",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "The Corporation announced the planned closure of the Fife Ethylene Plant, with shutdown activities expected to be completed in 2026.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Fife Ethylene Plant Planned Closure",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In Angola, a total of 1.6 net acres were relinquished and Block 15 amended its Production Sharing Agreement to extend the production license to 2037.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Angola Block 15 PSA Extension to 2037",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "risk_factor",
            "content": "In addition, proved reserves could be affected by an extended period of low prices which could reduce the level of the Corporation's capital spending and also impact our partners' capacity to fund their share of joint projects.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Proved Reserves Low Oil Price Capital Spending Risk",
            "entity_type_entity": "Risk",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2"
            },
            "chunk_type": "risk_factor",
            "content": "Proved undeveloped reserves in Australia and the United Arab Emirates have remained undeveloped for five years or more primarily due to constraints on the capacity of infrastructure, as well as the time required to complete development for very large projects. The Corporation is reasonably certain that these proved reserves will be produced; however, the timing and amount recovered can be affected by a number of factors including completion of development projects, reservoir performance, regulatory approvals, government policies, consumer preferences, the pace of co-venturer/government funding, changes in the amount and timing of capital investments, and significant changes in crude oil and natural gas price levels.",
            "entity_name": "XOM Proved Undeveloped Reserves Infrastructure and Development Timing Risk",
            "entity_type_entity": "Risk",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_2",
              "update_type": "confirmation"
            },
            "chunk_type": "guidance",
            "content": "Worldwide, we are contractually committed to deliver approximately 73 million barrels of oil and 2.9 trillion cubic feet of natural gas for the period from 2026 through 2028. We expect to fulfill the majority of these delivery commitments with production from our proved developed reserves.",
            "entity_name": "XOM 2026-2028 Oil and Gas Contractual Delivery Commitments",
            "entity_type_entity": "GuidanceUpdate",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
